Subject: [PATCH] A request thread passes the request on, never the line's tail
 (5347)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In threads 54282 and 54284 the person asked wrote "ask Sandro in my name"
and "you could ask Lasha to introduce". The server's own send cut the words
after the name and sent them as the whole question: asks 22447 ("ჩემი
სახელით.") and 22448 ("გააცნოს."), each under a new goal titled from the
line. In a request thread the server no longer writes that question: the
refused plan stays refused for the run to ask with the request, and the
last-chance send says plainly that nothing went.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
